    "result_text": "All clean. The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate owner duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**The key** \u2014 `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + householdId`:\n- `normalizedTelephone`: E.164 form\n- email: lower-cased, or empty when absent\n- `householdId`: the owner's shared-household identifier, empty when it belongs to no shared household\n\nRejection is a 409 **only when a new owner's whole key equals an existing owner's**. Because telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed \u2014 exactly as specified.\n\n**What I added:**\n- `OwnerIdentityKey` \u2014 derives the key for a request (`forRequest`, using the household id the request *would* be assigned) and for a stored owner (`forOwner`), so the check-time key matches the saved/returned key.\n- `Household` \u2014 shared household resolution/assignment, so `AssignHousehold` and the identity key use the exact same household id.\n- `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` \u2014 the single pipeline step; scans `findAll()` and throws `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (\u2192 409) on a full-key match.\n- `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` + handler + escalation YAML.\n- `identityKey` as a read-only field on the `Owner` schema (`openapi.yml`) plus a MapStruct expression, so it's **returned** in the response.\n\n**What I changed/removed:**\n- `owners.POST.yml`: replaced `checkTelephoneUnique`/`checkEmailUnique`/`checkHouseholdUnique` with one `checkIdentityUnique` step.\n- Deleted the three old check classes, their three exceptions, three handlers, and three escalation YAMLs.\n- Simplified `AssignHousehold` to delegate to `Household`.\n\n**Behaviour change (as required):** same last-name+address alone (or same email alone, or same telephone alone) no longer conflicts \u2014 only an exact full-key match does.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreRejectsIdentityCollision`) and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: the build regenerates DTOs from `openapi.yml`, so `OwnerDto` now carries `identityKey` (verified in the create response, e.g. `\"identityKey\":\"+61400000004||F113BD0AC223D30D\"`).",
